From: Guohan Lu <securely1g@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Parse pkg-config fields independently of separator whitespace

Debian's xtables.pc separates fields with colon-tabs, so looking for ": "
skips Name, Libs and Cflags. The resulting development-library target loses
its include roots, and native iproute2 consumers cannot find xtables headers.

Use the first ":" or "=" to distinguish fields from variables, and trim
boundary whitespace. Values retain embedded separators, including URLs in
variables and -DNAME=value compiler flags.

Source: https://github.com/bazel-contrib/rules_distroless/blob/v0.9.4/apt/private/pkgconfig.bzl
Origin: SONiC-maintained compatibility fix for upstream v0.9.4.

--- a/apt/private/pkgconfig.bzl
+++ b/apt/private/pkgconfig.bzl
@@ -42,16 +42,21 @@
     variables = {}
     directives = {}
     for l in pc.splitlines():
+        l = l.strip()
         if l.startswith("#"):
             continue
-        if not l.strip():
+        if not l:
             continue
-        if l.find(": ") != -1:
+        colon = l.find(":")
+        equals = l.find("=")
+        # A variable value may contain ":"; a field value may contain "=".
+        # The first separator determines which syntax this line uses.
+        if colon != -1 and (equals == -1 or colon < equals):
             (k, v) = _split_once(l, ":")
-            directives[k] = _expand_value(v.removeprefix(" "), variables)
-        elif l.find("=") != -1:
+            directives[k.strip()] = _expand_value(v.strip(), variables)
+        elif equals != -1:
             (k, v) = _split_once(l, "=")
-            variables[k] = _expand_value(v, variables)
+            variables[k.strip()] = _expand_value(v.strip(), variables)
 
     return (directives, variables)
 
